                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_08\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes a single line in TetrisPanel.java:\n  - private static final int HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";\n  + private static final String HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";\n\nThis was a build error: a String literal was being assigned to a field declared with type `int`, which will not compile in Java.\n\nSearching the candidates for the origin of this field shows it does not exist before candidate_08. In candidate_08, TetrisPanel.java is refactored to extract several hardcoded literals (window size, grid size, colors, filenames, etc.) into named static final constants, replacing the previous hardcoded string literal \"TetrisHighScores.txt\" used directly in `new File(...)` and `new FileWriter(...)` calls. During this refactor, the new constant was introduced as:\n  private static final int HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";\n\nThis is the exact same line (down to whitespace) that the fix commit corrects, confirming candidate_08 is where the bug was introduced. Candidate_09 is the fix commit itself, correcting the type from `int` to `String`. No other candidate touches this declaration, so candidate_08 is unambiguously the bug-introducing commit.\n"
